    "version": 1,
    "description": "Prioritizes candidates that preserve the remaining contact graph: fewer newly created components and isolated remainder nodes score higher. As a tie-break, favors lower contact degree, then smaller volume fraction when available. This is a weak structural heuristic, not a learned causal predictor: observations are limited and chains with unknown outcomes are not treated as scored failures.",
